DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       _N_o_t_e: this page describes the raw Linux  system  call  interface.   The
       wrapper  function  provided  by  _l_i_b_a_i_o  uses  a different type for the
       _c_t_x___i_d argument.  See VERSIONS.

       The iioo__ggeetteevveennttss() system call attempts to read at least _m_i_n___n_r  events
       and up to _n_r events from the completion queue of the AIO context speci‐
       fied by _c_t_x___i_d.

       The  _t_i_m_e_o_u_t  argument specifies the amount of time to wait for events,
       and is specified as a relative timeout in a ttiimmeessppeecc(3) structure.

       The specified time will be rounded up to the system  clock  granularity
       and is guaranteed not to expire early.

       Specifying  _t_i_m_e_o_u_t  as  NULL  means  block indefinitely until at least
       _m_i_n___n_r events have been obtained.

